# 2. REAL-TIME DATA ARCHITECTURE

Ensure complete and correct integration between:

**Backend → APIs → Hooks → SSE/WebSockets → State Management → Frontend Components**

The implementation must be properly wired end-to-end.

### Requirements

* Connect every metric and visualization to the appropriate backend source.
* Implement production-ready React hooks for all required data.
* Implement SSE for real-time telemetry/events where appropriate.
* Automatically update affected UI components when backend data changes.
* Handle connection lifecycle correctly.
* Handle reconnects and transient failures.
* Prevent duplicate SSE connections.
* Prevent memory leaks.
* Properly unsubscribe/cleanup listeners.
* Display connection status where useful.
* Provide graceful loading, empty, stale, and error states.
* Ensure real-time events invalidate or refresh affected cached data.
* Avoid unnecessary polling when SSE/event streaming is available.
* Maintain tenant isolation at every data layer.

Example architecture:

```text
Scanner / Agents / Cloud Connectors
              ↓
        Backend Services
              ↓
        Event / Telemetry Layer
              ↓
       REST / API / SSE
              ↓
       React Query / Hooks
              ↓
       Dashboard State
              ↓
     Real-Time UI Components
```

